## Description

If the following method is invoked by passing in the type stored in the custom attribute retrieved through reflection, it freezes the app:
```cs
    [MyCustomAttribute (typeof (MyType))]
    public object? TestCase (Type type)
    {
        if (type == typeof (MyType))
            return new MyType ();
        return null;
    }
```

Disassembly shows infinite loop at `0x1000f08a4` on `osx-arm64`:
```
00000001000f0880 <_TestHang_TestFixture__TestCase>:
1000f0880: a9bf7bfd    	stp	x29, x30, [sp, #-16]!
1000f0884: 910003fd    	mov	x29, sp
1000f0888: d0000800    	adrp	x0, 0x1001f2000 <_S_P_TypeLoader_Internal_TypeSystem_LockFreeReaderHashtableOfPointers_2<S_P_CoreLib_System_RuntimeTypeHandle__S_P_CoreLib_System_RuntimeTypeHandle>__Expand+0x70>
1000f088c: 912b4000    	add	x0, x0, #2768
1000f0890: eb00003f    	cmp	x1, x0
1000f0894: 54000080    	b.eq	0x1000f08a4 <_TestHang_TestFixture__TestCase+0x24>
1000f0898: aa1f03e0    	mov	x0, xzr
1000f089c: a8c17bfd    	ldp	x29, x30, [sp], #16
1000f08a0: d65f03c0    	ret
1000f08a4: 14000000    	b	0x1000f08a4 <_TestHang_TestFixture__TestCase+0x24>
```

## Repro

1. Download / install `.NET 9 preview 7`
2. Create console app 
```
dotnet new console --aot -n "TestHang"
```
3. Edit `Program.cs` in the following way:
```cs
using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;
using System.Reflection;

var testFixtureType = typeof(TestFixture);
var methods = testFixtureType.GetMethods()
    .Where(m => m.GetCustomAttributes(typeof(MyCustomAttribute), false).Any())
    .ToArray();

if (methods.Length > 0)
{
    MethodInfo method = methods[0];
    MyCustomAttribute? attribute = method.GetCustomAttribute<MyCustomAttribute>();
    if (attribute != null)
    {
        Type paramType = attribute.ParamType;
        TestFixture instance = new TestFixture();
        var result = instance.TestCase(paramType);
        Console.WriteLine(result);
    }
    else
    {
        Console.WriteLine("MyCustomAttribute not found on method");
    }
}
else
{
    Console.WriteLine("No methods found with MyCustomAttribute");
}

public class TestFixture
{
    [MyCustomAttribute (typeof (MyType))]
    public object? TestCase (Type type)
    {
        if (type == typeof (MyType))
            return new MyType ();
        return null;
    }
}

public class MyCustomAttribute : Attribute
{
    public Type ParamType { get; }
    public MyCustomAttribute(Type paramType)
    {
        ParamType = paramType;
    }
}

public class MyType  
{
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```
4. Publish / run the app

## Expected behavior

The app prints `MyType`.

## Actual behavior

The app hangs.

## Workaround

Root `MyType` in some way.

## Regression

Yes. .NET 9 preview 5 does not have this problem.

## Additional notes

Going back through changes it seems like this has been introduced with: https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/commit/9c7ee976fd771c183e98cf629e3776bba4e45ccc

This was initially discovered in Xamarin monotouch-test testing where such pattern is used for NUnit testing (reported in: https://github.com/xamarin/xamarin-macios/issues/20972).
